From: Marcin Krystianc <marcin.krystianc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SUNRPC: remove redundant tk_action updates in rpc_decode_header()

rpc_decode_header() sets tk_action to call_encode before it returns
-EAGAIN, on the out_garbage path and for AUTH_BADCRED or AUTH_BADVERF.
Its only caller, call_decode(), sets tk_action to call_encode again in
its -EAGAIN case, and nothing reads tk_action in between.

The assignment in call_decode() was added by commit cea57789e408
("SUNRPC: Clean up"). The one path that returned -EAGAIN with a
different tk_action was given its own return value, -EKEYREJECTED, by
commit 7987b694ade8 ("SUNRPC: Fix a use after free when a server
rejects the RPCSEC_GSS credential"). Since then the two assignments in
rpc_decode_header() have had no effect.

No functional change.

---
--- a/net/sunrpc/clnt.c
+++ b/net/sunrpc/clnt.c
@@ -2838,7 +2838,6 @@ out_garbage:
 	clnt->cl_stats->rpcgarbage++;
 	if (task->tk_garb_retry) {
 		task->tk_garb_retry--;
-		task->tk_action = call_encode;
 		return -EAGAIN;
 	}
 out_err:
@@ -2904,7 +2903,6 @@ out_msg_denied:
 			break;
 		task->tk_garb_retry--;
 		trace_rpc__bad_creds(task);
-		task->tk_action = call_encode;
 		return -EAGAIN;
 	case rpc_autherr_tooweak:
 		trace_rpc__auth_tooweak(task);
